    <!-- The guide's fourth chapter, landed with the screen it is about -->
    <string name="guide_alerts_title">How the alerts work</string>
    <string name="guide_alerts_p1">The ready-made ones are switches: severe weather ahead, rain in the next hours, the morning summary. Next to each one is written exactly what it sends and when, so nothing arrives that you did not ask for.</string>
    <string name="guide_alerts_p2">Then there are yours. Each one is a sentence with three pieces to tap: what to watch, how to compare it, the threshold. “Try it now” runs it on the data the app already has and tells you what it would have done, without sending anything.</string>
    <string name="guide_alerts_p3">The checks travel with the weather updates, at the same rhythm, so alerts cost no extra battery. And the message of an alert of yours is yours: Chiaro never rewrites it and never translates it.</string>
</resources>
